Package: bmbeR
Title: Prior-Focused Bayesian Model Building and Evaluation for 'rstanarm'
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("elkronos", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "jchase.msu@gmail.com")
Description: A prior-centred Bayesian workflow for regression models fitted
    with 'rstanarm'. Provides validated prior specifications, defensible
    data-informed priors (unit-information priors, Kass and Wasserman (1995)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1995.10476592>; parametric empirical Bayes
    shrinkage, Morris (1983) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1983.10477914>; power
    priors from historical data, Ibrahim and Chen (2000)
    <doi:10.1214/ss/1009212673>), prior predictive checks, modern MCMC
    convergence diagnostics (rank-normalised R-hat and bulk/tail effective
    sample size, Vehtari et al. (2021) <doi:10.1214/20-BA1221>), prior and
    likelihood sensitivity analysis by power-scaling without refitting
    (Kallioinen et al. (2023) <doi:10.1007/s11222-023-10366-5>), predictive
    evaluation with proper scoring rules (Gneiting and Raftery (2007)
    <doi:10.1198/016214506000001437>), and a reporting checklist aligned with
    the Bayesian Analysis Reporting Guidelines (Kruschke (2021)
    <doi:10.1038/s41562-021-01177-7>).
